  "boundary": "Exact static registration/module/token and six MethodSpec/type joins under the selected GameAssembly+metadata hash gate. Direct selected normal/null source order supports structural-only framing. TargetSettings uses buff_ec_native.json and finite selector extensions in buff_b2_native.json. GameplayTagQuery uses the member-two scalar32/count-times-four consumer in buff_b4_native.json; the output value occupies sixteen bytes but that store is not its variable wire extent. Finder18 additionally joins the selected dispatch entry and type-usage chain under the existing EC finder dispatcher. Its member-eleven reader selects ColliderShapeData, whose member-sixteen layout is distinct from HitBoxFinder ShapeData in buff_b2_native.json. Three exact UnityEngine.Vector3 contexts call the pinned twelve-byte source helper, not the variable blackboard vector profile. Four-byte float-helper results and other scalar bits remain anonymous. String helpers reuse the bounded byte-payload length/advance proof; byte decoding remains unresolved. Output setters and wrapper allocation do not supply source members. Unknown nested tags, deeper target recursion, live provider selection, allocation/refill/error parity, field/gameplay meaning and whole-BuffData EOF remain unresolved."
